    "result_text": "The full test suite is green \u2014 **32 tests, 0 failures, 0 errors, BUILD SUCCESS**, including the target `Cp21Tests`.\n\n## What I did\n\nThe spec required that on a successful owner create, an audit line be emitted via the logger named `AUDIT` carrying the owner id, `customerCode`, and `registrationDate`. In `OwnerRestControllerV1`:\n\n1. **Added a dedicated SLF4J logger** named `AUDIT` (`LoggerFactory.getLogger(\"AUDIT\")`) \u2014 the exact logger name the test's `AuditLogCapture` attaches its appender to.\n2. **Emitted the audit line immediately after `saveOwner(owner)`** in `addOwner`, once the owner id has been assigned:\n   ```java\n   AUDIT.info(\"owner created id={} customerCode={} registrationDate={}\",\n       owner.getId(), owner.getCustomerCode(), owner.getRegistrationDate());\n   ```\n\nPlacing it after the save (rather than earlier) ensures the id is present and the line is only written on the CREATED path \u2014 not on any of the earlier bad-request/conflict short-circuit returns. The formatted message contains all three values as strings, satisfying `audit.anyContains(id, customerCode, registrationDate)`.",
